# .mailmap — git-display author consolidation.
#
# Maps secondary author identities to the canonical one. Affects:
#   - `git log --use-mailmap` (default in modern git)
#   - `git shortlog`
#   - GitHub's Contributors graph
#
# Does NOT alter commit objects — historical authorship metadata is
# preserved in git history. This file is a display-time transformation
# only, so it's non-destructive (unlike `git filter-repo`).
#
# Format: <canonical-name> <canonical-email> <commit-name> <commit-email>

# Claude Code commits (historical, before 2026-05-17) — Co-Authored-By
# trailers from past sessions get attributed to the canonical author
# rather than appearing as a separate contributor.
#
# Note: GitHub's Contributors graph specifically does NOT honor .mailmap
# for Co-Authored-By trailers — only for the primary author field. So
# this mapping fixes `git shortlog --use-mailmap` and the GitHub profile
# page, but does NOT remove "Claude" from the repo's Contributors
# sidebar widget. To remove Claude from that widget, history must be
# rewritten (git filter-branch --msg-filter ...) + force-pushed.
